00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:48,000
You wouldn't want to meet these pinheads in an alley.

2
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Kingpin is a comedy film directed by Bobby Farrelly.

3
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:12,000
After bowler Roy Munson swindles the wrong crowd and is left with a
hook for a hand, he settles into impoverished obscurity.

4
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:54,000
That is, until he uncovers the next big thing: an Amish kid named Ishmael.

5
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
So, the corrupt and the hopelessly naive hit the circuit
intent on settling an old score with Big Ern.

6
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Roy Munson, played by Woody Harrelson.

7
00:39:54,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Ishmael Boorg, played by Randy Quaid.

8
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:42,000
Claudia, played by Vanessa Angel.

9
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:24,000
Ernie McCracken, played by Bill Murray.

10
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
The Gambler, played by Chris Elliott.

11
01:02:42,000 --> 01:02:48,000
Mr. Boorg, played by William Jordan.

12
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:30,000
Kingpin is a 1996 American sports comedy film directed by Peter and
Bobby Farrelly and written by Barry Fanaro and Mort Nathan.

13
01:14:06,000 --> 01:14:12,000
Starring Woody Harrelson, Randy Quaid, Vanessa Angel and Bill Murray, it tells the story of an alcoholic
ex-professional bowler (Harrelson) who becomes the manager for a promising Amish talent (Quaid).

14
01:19:48,000 --> 01:19:54,000
It was filmed in and around Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, as a
stand-in for Scranton, Amish country, and Reno, Nevada.

15
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film was produced by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, Motion Picture Corporation of America
and Rysher Entertainment and released by MGM/UA Distribution Co.

16
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
on July 26, 1996, with a budget of $25 million.

17
01:36:54,000 --> 01:37:00,000
The film received mixed reviews and grossed $32.2 million.

18
01:42:36,000 --> 01:42:42,000
The film explores themes of sports, stripper,
handicap, sexual favor, star spangled banner.

19
01:48:18,000 --> 01:48:24,000
The tone is lighthearted.
